istening  i've spoken for maybe a total of two two  and a half hours however there is no  doubt in my mind and judy huns said the  same  my ability to speak to express myself in  korean has improved noticeably just  after three weeks  has improved noticeably compared to when  we last spoke and that basically all  comes from those three weeks of  intensive input  based learning so i've said this before  you can't speak your way to fluency you  eventually have to speak a lot but you  have to listen and read your way  to familiarity with the language to  vocabulary so that you can then when you  start to speak you have something to say  you understand what people are saying my  comprehension is so much better than it  was the last time i spoke to jooheon i  understood most of what she was saying  wonderful i struggled to say what i  wanted to say i was looking for words  occasionally a japanese a japanese word  popped in there what i find is when i'm  trying to speak korean i either go to  japanese in my head  because the word order is the same  and it's a language that i speak much  much better so  were you know languages with that word  order my brain says it's got to be  japanese and of course the last language  that i studied was czech so the other  thing my brain tends to do is oh you're  struggling with the language it'll go to  check so i have to fight that and try  and stay on korean  and so i will simply continue what i'm  doing uh massive listing and reading  which i can fit in like even today i'll  end up with three hours because i had  probably over an hour in the car and i  did a bit of reading this morning i did  a bit of reading this afternoon i'm  gonna do a bit more reading tonight so  it'll end up being three hours so you  can always find the time during the day  but you gotta stay with it even if you  don't have a lot of time you got to  continue doing it and sometimes it's  tough you're tired you'd like to do  other things  and normally i would do other things i  would limit myself probably to an hour  but i'm committed to this 90-day  challenge so i'm trying to push it up to  three hours a day  grinding away  and i'm hoping  that in a week two three weeks from now  or even  at the end of it i will be speaking even  better but most of my activity will be  listening and reading although i may  step up my speaking in another couple of  weeks  anyway that's my comment for
 

